::ENG4_U02_L02_GP_Q01::[MLA.ENG4.R.02] Passage: When the council gathered to vote on closing the old reading room, Elias sat in the back beside the empty chair his mother had used every Thursday. The room smelled of paper, dust, and raincoats. On the wall, a cracked photograph showed children holding library cards like small flags. Several council members argued that the building was inefficient and that a digital archive would serve more people. Elias agreed that the town needed better access, yet he kept looking at the empty chair. When his turn came to speak, he did not ask the council to preserve every shelf. Instead, he asked them to carry the reading room's promise into whatever came next: a place where no child had to enter knowledge alone. Which pair best states two themes? {
~A. Chairs and photographs#These are topics or objects, not themes.
~B. Dust and raincoats#These are details, not themes.
=C. Communities should honor meaningful traditions, and progress should preserve human purpose.#Correct. These are thematic insights.
~D. Councils always make wrong decisions#The passage does not support this absolute claim.
}
::ENG4_U02_L02_GP_Q02::[MLA.ENG4.R.02] Passage: Elias agreed that the town needed better access, yet he kept looking at the empty chair. What does this detail show about theme development? {
~A. Elias rejects all change.#He agrees better access is needed.
=B. The passage complicates the conflict by showing Elias values both access and memory.#Correct. The detail develops two themes together.
~C. Elias forgets the reading room's past.#He keeps looking at the chair.
~D. The council stops debating.#This is not stated.
}
::ENG4_U02_L02_GP_Q03::[MLA.ENG4.R.01] Passage: On the wall, a cracked photograph showed children holding library cards like small flags. What is the functional significance of the photograph? {
=A. It shows the reading room's history and the public value of access to knowledge.#Correct. It supports memory and access themes.
~B. It proves the building is new.#The photograph is cracked and historical.
~C. It shows Elias dislikes children.#This is not supported.
~D. It removes the theme of memory.#It supports memory.
}
::ENG4_U02_L02_GP_Q04::[MLA.ENG4.R.10] Passage: Instead, he asked them to carry the reading room's promise into whatever came next: a place where no child had to enter knowledge alone. Which paraphrase is accurate? {
~A. Elias asks the council to keep every shelf exactly as it is.#This contradicts the passage.
~B. Elias says children should avoid knowledge.#This contradicts the passage.
~C. Elias asks the council to close every library permanently.#This is not stated.
=D. Elias asks the council to preserve the reading room's purpose in the future.#Correct
}
::ENG4_U02_L02_GP_Q05::[MLA.ENG4.V.01] Passage: Several council members argued that the building was inefficient and that a digital archive would serve more people. What does inefficient mean in this context? {
~A. Emotionally meaningful#That is not the meaning here.
=B. Not using resources effectively#Correct
~C. Historically important#This is a different idea.
~D. Full of books#This does not define inefficient.
}
